---
title: "Columns Tool Panel - Customisation"
enterprise: true
---

Customise how columns appear in the Columns Tool Panel: their styling and names, custom labels, the context menu and the drag image.

## Styling & Naming Columns

Style columns in the tool panel with `toolPanelClass`, and give them a different name there with `headerValueGetter`.

The example below demonstrates both. Note the following:

- The `gold`, `silver` and `bronze` columns are styled using `toolPanelClass`.
- The country column uses a `headerValueGetter` to show a different name in the tool panel, the drop zones and the grid header. Drag it into the Row Groups section to see the drop zone name.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tool Panel Styling" name="styling"  exampleHeight=610 /%}

To add a CSS class to a column in the tool panel, set `toolPanelClass` on its column definition:

```{% frameworkTransform=true spaceBetweenProperties=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        // set as string
        { field: 'gold', toolPanelClass: 'tp-gold' },

        // set as array of strings
        { field: 'silver', toolPanelClass: ['tp-silver'] },

        // set as function returning string or array of strings
        {
            field: 'bronze',
            toolPanelClass: params => {
                return 'tp-bronze';
            },
        }
    ]
}
```

To give a column a different name in the tool panel, use a [`headerValueGetter`](./column-headers/#header-value-getters) and return the name when `params.location` is `'columnToolPanel'`:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        {
            field: 'country',
            headerValueGetter: params => params.location === 'columnToolPanel' ? 'Country (TP)' : 'Country',
        }
    ]
}
```

## Custom Column Labels

Use `columnLabelRenderer` to replace the text shown for columns and column groups in the Columns section. The grid continues to provide and manage the checkbox, drag handle and group expand controls.

Supply the renderer directly, or reference a name registered in the grid's [`components`](./components/#registering-custom-components) map. Pass additional properties through `columnLabelRendererParams`.

Use `columnLabelRendererSelector` to select different renderers for individual columns or column groups. The selector can also provide renderer-specific `params`; returning `undefined` falls back to `columnLabelRenderer`.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    components: {
        customColumnLabel: CustomColumnLabel,
    },
    sideBar: {
        toolPanels: [{
            id: 'columns',
            labelDefault: 'Columns',
            labelKey: 'columns',
            iconKey: 'columns',
            toolPanel: 'agColumnsToolPanel',
            toolPanelParams: {
                columnLabelRenderer: 'customColumnLabel',
                columnLabelRendererParams: {
                    columnIcon: '●',
                    columnGroupIcon: '◆',
                },
            },
        }],
    },
};
```

The renderer receives either `column` or `columnGroup`, together with the resolved `displayName` and a `source` of `'columnsToolPanel'`. The same renderer can be configured independently for the [Column Chooser](./column-chooser/#custom-column-labels).

{% note %}
Column search, tooltips, drag labels and accessibility announcements continue to use `displayName`, rather than text extracted from the renderer. Column selection rows have a fixed height, so renderer content should remain inline and fit within the configured list item height. Clicking the rendered label retains the normal selection behaviour; interactive elements should stop event propagation when they should not toggle the column.
{% /note %}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Column Labels" name="custom-column-labels" exampleHeight=610 /%}

